From: local
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: retimestamp incoming audio from zero

Using appsrc do-timestamp while the MediaStream player is still completing its
asynchronous state change can produce absolute monotonic-clock PTS values. A
synchronized audio sink then waits for those far-future timestamps, and the
upstream appsrc queue fills.

Keep the existing do-timestamp path for incoming video. For incoming audio,
copy the encoded buffer and assign timestamps relative to the first local
monotonic timestamp. This starts the audio stream at PTS zero and preserves
real-time packet spacing.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
@@
-                GST_BUFFER_PTS(buffer.get()) = GST_CLOCK_TIME_NONE;
-                GST_BUFFER_DTS(buffer.get()) = GST_CLOCK_TIME_NONE;
+                if (m_isVideoTrack) {
+                    GST_BUFFER_PTS(buffer.get()) = GST_CLOCK_TIME_NONE;
+                    GST_BUFFER_DTS(buffer.get()) = GST_CLOCK_TIME_NONE;
+                } else {
+                    auto now = gst_util_get_timestamp();
+                    if (!GST_CLOCK_TIME_IS_VALID(m_retimestampOrigin))
+                        m_retimestampOrigin = now;
+                    GST_BUFFER_PTS(buffer.get()) = now - m_retimestampOrigin;
+                    GST_BUFFER_DTS(buffer.get()) = GST_BUFFER_PTS(buffer.get());
+                }
@@
-            "do-timestamp", isCaptureTrack || m_retimestampIncomingMedia, "handle-segment-change", TRUE, nullptr);
+            "do-timestamp", isCaptureTrack || (m_retimestampIncomingMedia && m_isVideoTrack),
+            "handle-segment-change", TRUE, nullptr);
@@
     bool m_retimestampIncomingMedia { false };
+    GstClockTime m_retimestampOrigin { GST_CLOCK_TIME_NONE };
